DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("ln((x*3))");
$fun_1 = Formula("7/((ln((1*x))))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("(5, infinity) U (5, infinity)");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("(5, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-8, -7, -3, 2, 9}) U {-8, -7, -3, 2, 9}");
$set_ans_6 = Compute("{-8, -7, -3, 2, 9} U (5, infinity)");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("({-10, -9, -7, 5, 7} - ({-9, -1, 3, 4, 9} U (3, infinity)))");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("({-9, -1, 3, 4, 9} - {-9, -1, 3, 4, 9})");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("(3, infinity) U (3, infinity) U {-10, -9, -7, 5, 7} U {-9, -1, 3, 4, 9}");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

[`1+16+0-2`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>Formula('15'),width=>4}
---

What is the value of [`6+5+6-1*17`]? [_____]{answer=>Formula('0'),width=>10}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-9, -1, 3, 4, 9\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x > 2\}`]
- [`C = \{-10, -9, -7, 5, 7\}`]

Compute:
- [`C - (A \cup B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`A - A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`B \cup B \cup C \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x > 4\}`]
- [`B = \{-8, -7, -3, 2, 9\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`A \cap B \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}
- [`B \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_6}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -4, 5, 4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -1, -7, -8 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-4, 5, 4>") . Compute("<-1, -7, -8>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-4, 5, 4>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-4, 5, 4>") x Compute("<-1, -7, -8>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-4, 5, 4>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-1, -7, -8>") . Compute("<-4, 5, 4>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-1, -7, -8>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 7, -1, 5 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 5, -1, -2 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<7, -1, 5>") x Compute("<5, -1, -2>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<7, -1, 5>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<7, -1, 5>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<5, -1, -2>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<5, -1, -2>") x Compute("<7, -1, 5>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<7, -1, 5>"))}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>2)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>9)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(6) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>6)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
